// PinglyMotion Script Lab - help for each RLV command of the behaviour table (lane 1, job R3)
//
// RLV_HELP(name, example, sentence): one row for every behaviour of Rlv::behaviours() and for the
// four families (setdebug_, setenv_, getdebug_, getenv_), in the table's order.
//  - example: one whole RLV line in our own words. tests/tst_rlvexamples.cpp checks that every
//    example parses, names its own command, and passes the table's checks and C's option check
//    (in RLVa mode; in plain RLV mode for the commands only RLV has).
//  - sentence: what the command does in Second Life, in plain words for a beginner, at most 12
//    words (the same test checks the count and the avoided words of docs/TEACHING.md).
// The table's own description (rlvbehaviours.cpp) stays as it is: it also says what the sandbox
// does, and tests/tst_rlvsources.cpp reads the table.
//
// The keys in the examples are made up (a1b2c3d4-...); they are no real avatar or object.
//
